  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect- Entreprise and Business Development - Enterprise and Business Development</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect- Entreprise and Business Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable economic development of vulnerable groups comprising of women, men and youth small holder producers to economically empowered and innovative entrepreneurs</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is aimed at strengthening partner organisations to enable them to create sustainable economic development for specific          vulnerable groups (men, women and youth) facilitaing the creation of  employment, through self help and practical tools which strengthen    the individual and society for sustainable development</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect has applied to Sida for funding of  SEK 17 013 000,00 to carry out the &quot;Enterprise and Business Development Programme &quot; in Zimbabwe during the period 1st October 2014 - 30 September 2017. 

The intervention seeks to economically empower communities by creating employment through small to medium entreprises thereby improving livelihoods. We Effect  will partner with three local organisations through which they will implement the programme.  The partner organisations are Zimbabwe Women&apos;s Bureau; Self Help Development Foundation (SHDF); Jekesa Pfungwa/Vulingqondo (JPV)
The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is 42.4 million SEK, out of which the Organisation&#x2019;s own funding is approximately 1.8 million SEK  and the remaining is contributed by  Radio Fund  SEK3.6; Civsam SEK14.5 ; Postcode SEK5.3</narrative>
  </description>
